  "question": "What rules should I follow in the Kubernetes Slack?",
  "answer": "You should follow these rules in the Kubernetes Slack:\n\n- Conversations should stay on topic in each channel [1].\n- Abide by the Code of Conduct [1].\n- Use the community inviter to join the Kubernetes Slack [1].\n- Channels must be Kubernetes-related [2].\n- Small external projects should use relevant SIG or WG channels [2].\n- Use your best judgment when requesting a channel [2].\n- Avoid using `@all`, `@here`, and `@channel` commands unless necessary [3].\n- Channels should be dedicated to SIGs, WGs, sub-projects, or community topics [2].\n- Channels should be relevant to Kubernetes programs and projects [2].\n- Two Slack admins must review and agree to sponsor a channel [3].",
